From 765e8949b80e86bdf9430520b75d68d7bf88cf28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:24:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mp: finish the d1cars -> bake rename (dedi core_mods refused
 every client)

dediserver.example.json required core_mods [mp, carhacks, d1cars]. d1cars was
renamed bake, so no client ever reports it and mods_match() refused everyone at
mod_check >= 1 (the example's own setting). The core list is now
[mp, carhacks, bake]; bake is a core module, which the runtime force-enables, so
it is always in a client's manifest. Same rename in the dedi README, core.py
docstring, test_console.py, the e2e rig, the pack_lan packagers (the Micheal
packager hard-failed on the missing MODS/d1cars) and mp_session.c's log text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015LjSznjzjHgGhjQaMfW1Mq
